/**
 * HomePlacesDirectory — Yahoo / Craigslist-style link tree.
 *
 * Mike 2026-05-08: "for the homepage, still need some type of yahoo,
 * craigslist type of link tree to visit places."
 *
 * Then 2026-05-08 (later): "lets have this list include every /, /gandalf, etc"
 * — comprehensive index of every public route on the site, organized
 * by purpose.
 *
 * Then 2026-05-08 (later still): "as new / are added, can you make sure
 * they get added to bottom menu" — so the directory is now HYBRID:
 *
 *   1. The 14 hand-curated SECTIONS below stay opinionated. New routes
 *      should still be moved into the right category by editing this
 *      file — that's what keeps the shape readable.
 *   2. A 15th UNFILED section is auto-discovered at build time. We
 *      glob src/pages/, diff against the curated href set, and surface
 *      anything new at the bottom. Nothing slips through anymore.
 *
 * Filters applied to auto-discovery:
 *   - Skip dynamic routes ([slug], [id])
 *   - Skip /admin/* (operator-only)
 *   - Skip /404, /index (the home itself)
 *   - .astro / .md / .ts → route path; .json.ts stays as .json (so
 *     /agents.json shows up correctly if not already curated)
 *
 * The aesthetic is dense, terse, scannable. No images, no chrome, just
 * LINKS — the way Yahoo's portal looked in 1996 and Craigslist still
 * looks today. Most links are label-only; blurbs only on the most
 * notable items per section.
 *
 * Mounted on / between THIS WEEK and ARCHIVE TEASER.
 */

interface Place { href: string; label: string; blurb?: string; }
